result_text:
No CLAUDE.md rule applies to this C change; the user-level file only covers agent tooling. I couldn't compile a test because writing to /tmp needed a permission I don't have, so the first finding is based on C semantics. Its first two entries are one defect with two runtime effects.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "src/networking.c",
    "line": 2774,
    "summary": "The parenthesized `(\"fmt\", args...)` groups inside the ternary are comma-operator expressions, not argument lists, so in the non-redacted branch snprintf's format string becomes the last operand, `c->querybuf + sdslen(c->querybuf) - PROTO_DUMP_LEN/2`. That is attacker-controlled query-buffer data used as a format string, called with no arguments.",
    "failure_scenario": "hide-user-data-from-log=no (the default), verbosity is verbose, or the client is the primary. A client sends 128 or more unparsable bytes ending in `%s%s%s%n...` (for example an invalid mbulk count followed by padding). setProtocolError then calls snprintf(buf, 256, <user bytes>), which reads garbage varargs or writes via %n: remote memory disclosure or corruption, or a crash."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/networking.c",
    "line": 2772,
    "summary": "Same comma-operator bug in the redacted branch: the ternary's true operand evaluates to the size_t `sdslen(c->querybuf) - c->qb_pos`, which is converted to a pointer and passed as snprintf's format string.",
    "failure_scenario": "hide-user-data-from-log=yes and a client triggers a protocol error with at least 128 bytes pending (for example a 200-byte invalid inline request). snprintf gets format pointer (char*)200 and the server segfaults. Turning redaction on gives a remote DoS."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/networking.c",
    "line": 2771,
    "summary": "The ternary mixes an integer operand (size_t) with a pointer operand (char*), a pointer/integer type mismatch, and the left operands of the commas are discarded. The compiler warns (-Wunused-value, conditional type mismatch), but the build doesn't fail because WARN lacks -Werror, so the broken code ships silently.",
    "failure_scenario": "Building with the default WARN=-Wall -W prints 'left-hand operand of comma expression has no effect' and 'pointer/integer type mismatch in conditional expression', yet the binary still builds with the broken format handling described above."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/networking.c",
    "line": 2771,
    "summary": "Choosing between two complete format/argument sets with a ternary inside one snprintf call can't work in C. Use an explicit `if (server.hide_user_data_from_log) {...} else {...}` with a separate snprintf call in each branch, or check redaction once before the size branches.",
    "failure_scenario": "As written, both branches are wrong (see the first two findings). A single redaction check before building `buf`, like showLatestBacklog and logStackContent do, would be correct and simpler, and would avoid duplicating the redaction in two places."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/networking.c",
    "line": 2769,
    "summary": "The redaction is inconsistent between branches: the short-buffer branch logs only a constant 'Redacted' string with no byte count, while the long branch tries to log the byte count. It also uses a new marker style, '[hide_user_data_from_log]Redacted', rather than the existing 'hide-user-data-from-log is on, skip logging ...' wording.",
    "failure_scenario": "An operator grepping logs for the established 'hide-user-data-from-log is on' message misses these entries. Logs for short and long protocol errors carry different information under redaction."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/networking.c",
    "line": 2768,
    "summary": "No test covers the protocol-error log with hide-user-data-from-log enabled or with a buffer of 128 bytes or more, so the crash and format-string paths went unnoticed (tests/unit/protocol.tcl has no such case).",
    "failure_scenario": "Running the existing suite with the default `hide-user-data-from-log no` and short invalid requests never reaches the else-if branch with redaction on, so the segfault and format-string bug pass CI."
  }
]
```
